[stderr] +## Original-asset contract
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The asset language is the same original *matchday knowledge* studio described
[stderr] +in `01-creative-direction.md` and `04-experience-contract.md`: category fields,
[stderr] +pitch-line geometry, stat blocks, signal sweeps, and celebration shapes. It
[stderr] +must not become a stadium, club, competition, broadcaster, player, kit, crest,
[stderr] +or reference-product trade dress. This non-fiction trivia release has no
[stderr] +fictional characters, locations, dialogue portraits, maps, or gameplay worlds.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +IDs use `ASSET-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable once a package references
[stderr] +them. Variants append `-<state>-<size>` (for example,
[stderr] +`ASSET-FBK-001-correct-2x`); locale is a manifest field, not baked into a
[stderr] +universal visual. The asset manifest records ID, version, source/checksum,
[stderr] +owner, licence/provenance, alt-text/meaning, variants, and review status.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Every release asset is created for this project or has documented rights. Do
[stderr] +not trace, scrape, prompt for, or modify a reference screenshot, mark, kit,
[stderr] +photo, or distinctive layout. Generated output retains prompt/model/version
[stderr] +and gets human originality review; third-party material needs licence and
[stderr] +attribution review. Uncertain provenance, embedded unlocalisable essential
[stderr] +text, missing alt/meaning treatment, or failed contrast/state review rejects
[stderr] +the asset. Decorative absence may fall back gracefully; required UI/state
[stderr] +assets reject a release.
