ature-model.md-123-back visibly; missing audio leaves full text feedback; untranslated content is\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-124-not offered as a language. **Boundary:** original broadcast-inspired system\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-125-only; languages and exact audio asset count await approval.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-129-**Entities/lifecycle:** `ContentVersion` draft \u2192 validated \u2192 staged \u2192 active \u2192\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-130-rolled-back; `DiagnosticEvent` queued \u2192 consented/withheld \u2192 sent/discarded.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-131-**Rules:** version switch only between rounds; cache refresh protects confirmed\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:132:save; errors offer retry/home; diagnostics minimise data. **Authoring inputs:**\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:133:release manifest, compatibility declaration, test evidence, privacy/store copy.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-134-**Dependencies:** platform packaging/PWA cache, content, recovery. **Outcome:**\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-135-safe delivery on feasible networks. **Edge cases:** failed/partial update,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:136:offline cache, compatibility failure, error-report denial, and rollback are J5.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-137-**Boundary:** provider/CI/OS/browser matrix/performance and store policies await\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-138-approval; no live event operation.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-139-\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-142-| Capability | Responsive web | PWA | Android / iOS | Invariant |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-143-| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-144-| Quiz rules, cards, score, save semantics | Full shared core | Same | Same | No target-exclusive content or rule. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:145:| Input/layout | keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad; responsive phone/tablet/desktop | browser-supported subset | touch; orientation TBD | Every action has an accessible equivalent. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-146-| Offline/update | browser cache subject to approved support | install, explicit offline/cache-refresh UX | packaged/cache path subject to delivery choice | Cached compatible content and confirmed save survive offline/update. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:147:| Accessibility/localisation | semantic web controls | same shared settings | platform accessibility integrations | Same outcome; platform affordance may differ. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:148:| Packaging/diagnostics | web compatibility/consent | install/cache safety | store/privacy/thermal/battery/size requirements | Exact matrices/budgets/vendors are gated, never silently weakened. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-149-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-150-## Prioritised feature catalogue and slices\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-151-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-152-| Priority / slice | Features | User outcome / journeys | Dependencies |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-153-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:154:| P0 \u2014 first release | GAME-001\u2013012; 53 bounded original cards; tutorial + standard round; adjudication, score/streak, feedback; settings/accessibility; local save/recovery/delete; offline cached play; original feedback; versioned delivery/error UI | Complete J0\u2013J5 core; J1 has no deferred dependency. | Approved factual sources/bank size, target and packaging decisions where required. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:155:| P1 \u2014 later, approval required | Account identity, remote sync/conflict resolution, account deletion/retention, optional connected status | Cross-device return only after policy and backend approval. | Identity, privacy, security, outage and conflict policy. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:156:| P2 \u2014 deferred | Seasonal/live events, player-created/shared content, advanced analytics, advanced monetisation, purchases/entitlements, multiplayer/social features | New content/community/commercial outcomes, not core completion. | Operations, moderation/safety, store/refund, rights, and cost decisions. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-157-| Excluded | RPG campaign/battle/party; match simulation; copied reference expression | None; incompatible with discovered game identity. | None. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-158-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-159-## Open decisions retained for approval\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-161-Approve factual source/licensing policy and exact catalogue size; supported\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-162-OS/browser/device matrix, orientation, performance/battery/thermal/download\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-163-budgets; implementation/packaging stack and crash provider; language list and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:164:audio quantity; account/sync/safety/commerce/live-operation policies. These\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-165-gates do not prevent an offline local first tutorial once its original reviewed\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md-166-content and selected platform implementation exist.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-5-[feature model](02-feature-model.md), and [game design bible](02-game-design-bible.md).\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-6-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-7-This contract implements the bounded first-release football-trivia game. It\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:8:does not turn the brief's approval-gated account, multiplayer, live-service,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:9:commerce, or remote-sync requests into production scope. It specifies a\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-10-vendor-neutral architecture so those systems can be added only after their\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:11:identity, cost, safety, retention, and outage decisions are approved.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-12-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-13-## Production architecture and boundaries\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-14-\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-22-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-23-| Component / owned boundary | Product or quality requirement traced | Contract |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-24-| --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:25:| Quiz application shell | GAME-005/008/009; J0\u2013J3 | Owns routes, focus, pause/visibility prompts, ephemeral UI and accessible rendering. Sends intents to the core and never mutates a run directly. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:26:| Input and accessibility adapters | GAME-009/012; responsive web and phones | Map touch, pointer, keyboard, and gamepad to semantic actions (`navigate`, `select`, `submit`, `back`, `pause`). Apply text/contrast/reduced-motion/caption settings; unsupported hardware has a visible equivalent. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-27-| Deterministic quiz core | GAME-001, 003, 005\u2013008 | Owns selection, normalisation/adjudication, score/streak, milestones, legal lifecycle transitions, and versioned rule calculations. Explicit seed and rule version make selection/results reproducible. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-28-| Content registry and validator | GAME-001\u2013004; curated original bank | Resolves immutable published packages by stable ID and refuses invalid or withdrawn content before it can enter a new round. Runtime reads only validated data. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:29:| Save/recovery repository | GAME-008/010; J3 | Owns revisioned snapshots, checksum/validation, atomic promotion, rollback, migration, quarantine, export only if later approved, and confirmed deletion. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-30-| Release/cache manager | GAME-011/012; PWA/mobile offline delivery | Stages signed/hashed approved package and assets; activates only between rounds and never during a save commit. It retains a known-good compatible package on update failure. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:31:| Error boundary and diagnostics | crash recovery and privacy | Owns plain-language retry, return-home, and recovery choices. P0 diagnostics are local and consent-gated; no telemetry transport is assumed. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:32:| Editorial build tooling | J4/J5; factual/release integrity | Imports author-controlled source files, runs schema/relationship/provenance checks, and emits a content manifest. It has no runtime authoring or publishing endpoint. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-33-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-34-```text\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-35-authored content \u2500> build validator \u2500> immutable ContentPackage \u2500\u2510\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-36-                                                               \u251c\u2500> deterministic quiz core <\u2500 semantic input actions\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-37-platform renderer/accessibility <\u2500 state + events \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518             \u2502\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-38-             \u2502                                                               \u251c\u2500> save/recovery repository\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:39:             \u2514\u2500> release/cache manager (safe boundary only) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500> local error/diagnostic record\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-40-```\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-41-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-42-Only the core creates durable game facts. The shell owns transient selection,\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-48-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-49-| Data class | Owner and lifecycle | Local persistence/retention | Access, recovery, and authorization |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-50-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:51:| `ContentPackage` | Editorial owner: draft \u2192 review \u2192 published \u2192 staged \u2192 active \u2192 superseded/rolled back/withdrawn | Bundled or cached immutable release artifact; current compatible and last-known-good package follow platform cache policy | Player runtime reads only published package. No content write API, account role, or remote publish service exists in P0. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:52:| `LocalProfile`, settings | Player: new \u2192 active \u2192 deletion-pending \u2192 deleted; settings valid \u2192 applied \u2192 reset | Separate local records; retained until explicit profile deletion | Browser/device profile controls local access. Failed setting write retains the applied session value and explains it. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-53-| `RoundRun`, attempts, results, milestones | Core: created \u2192 active/paused \u2192 complete, abandoned, or recoverable; attempts presented \u2192 draft \u2192 submitted \u2192 resolved | Valid confirmed snapshots plus prior known-good revision; unresolved draft is disposable | Immutable resolved attempts reference exact content/rule versions. A player may recover/discard only their local state. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-54-| `SaveSnapshot`/recovery record | Repository: candidate \u2192 validated \u2192 confirmed \u2192 superseded/quarantined \u2192 deleted | Current confirmed revision and prior valid revision; recovery metadata is bounded and deleted with profile | No overwrite of a valid revision by a malformed candidate. Corruption/migration failure offers last valid snapshot or new game. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-55-| Original visual/audio assets and strings | Creative/content owner: source \u2192 provenance/review \u2192 manifest reference \u2192 packaged \u2192 superseded | Versioned content package references; source provenance retained in repository/release records | Runtime may resolve only manifest IDs. Missing optional cue gives text feedback; missing required asset rejects release. |\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-77-SaveSnapshot {\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-78-  schemaVersion, contentPackageId, contentVersion, ruleVersion, profileId,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-79-  revision, status, selectionSeed, roundRun, attempts[], scoreState,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:80:  milestones, repeatLedger, settingsRef, checksum, committedAt\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-81-}\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-82-```\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-83-\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-169-| Invalid/partial content/cache update | Keep compatible active package and save; block affected new-round route with retry/home explanation. Never activate it mid-round. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-170-| First offline visit/no cached package | Explain that initial approved download is needed; never misrepresent an uncached game as offline-ready. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-171-| Fault/crash loop | Error boundary offers retry, return home, and recovery; optional local diagnostics do not block either action. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:172:| Explicit deletion | Confirm scope, then remove profile/settings/history/snapshots/recovery records/local diagnostics and return to first launch. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-173-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-174-Migrations are pure, ordered `fromSchema \u2192 toSchema` transformations with\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-175-fixtures for each supported predecessor. They run into a new candidate,\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-177-retry cannot apply one twice. A migration cannot reinterpret old answer facts,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-178-grant new score/milestones, or change a completed run's content/rule reference.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-179-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:180:## Trust, privacy, security, and authorization\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-181-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:182:- P0 has no server-owned resource and no player account: there is therefore no\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:183:  remote authorization role. A device/browser-profile owner can alter local\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-184-  data; local persistence is integrity/recovery protection, not anti-cheat.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-185-  Editorial publication is an offline repository/release responsibility, not a\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-186-  client role. Any future server requires authenticated least-privilege roles,\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-188-  deletion/retention and outage/conflict policy before implementation.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-189-- Persist only necessary local profile, game state, preferences, compatible\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-190-  content/cache and bounded recovery data. Do not collect names, contact data,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:191:  precise location, ad IDs, payment data, account IDs, raw typed answers, or\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-192-  gameplay analytics. A diagnostic excludes question text, answer text, save\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-193-  payload and unique identity; consent describes fields, purpose, retention,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-194-  deletion, and any approved transport.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-210-| Contract | Responsive public web | PWA | Android phone | iPhone (iOS) |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-211-| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-212-| Shared code/data boundary | Shared core, schemas, package, actions, save semantics; web renderer/layout adapter only. | Same shared core/data; install/service-worker/cache adapter only. | Same shared core/data; native/web-runtime packaging, touch/accessibility/storage adapter only. | Same shared core/data; iOS packaging, touch/accessibility/storage adapter only. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:213:| Inputs/device capabilities | Keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad when exposed; resize/visibility; feature-detect all. | Same; install/notification/storage prompts optional and non-blocking. | Touch first; orientation choice TBD; respect system text, contrast, motion, audio and focus affordances. | Touch first; orientation choice TBD; respect system text, contrast, motion, audio and focus affordances. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-214-| Offline and recovery | Offline only after assets/package cached; first uncached visit explains network need. Local save is independent of cache. | Installable offline route after successful cache; known-good cache survives refresh failure; safe update notice. | Packaged/cache-approved content and independent local save; offline core works after first installation; update only safe boundary. | Same as Android, subject to platform storage/cache behaviour; retain confirmed save across package/content update. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:215:| Build and test | Hashed static bundle/manifest; core/content/save unit tests; browser layout, keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad, slow-network and error checks. | Adds manifest/service worker; test install, offline reload, cache rollback, update-safe-boundary, cache/storage pressure. | Signed store-compatible build after approval; test physical/emulated representative touch, interrupt/resume, storage pressure, accessibility, battery/thermal/size budget. | Signed store-compatible build after approval; test representative devices, interrupt/resume, storage pressure, accessibility, battery/thermal/size budget. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-216-| Accessibility/performance | Semantic labels, focus, text scaling, contrast, captions/non-colour cues; measure approved load/frame/memory/bundle budgets across phone/tablet/desktop. | Same plus offline/update/install state is fully operable; measure cold/warm/offline startup and cache size. | Touch target, screen reader, text scaling, reduced motion/captions; measure startup/frame/memory/download/battery/thermal against approved thresholds. | Equivalent outcome using platform assistive tech; measure same approved mobile budgets and interrupted-state recovery. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:217:| Release channel/policy | Approved immutable static host; selected staged rollout/rollback; publish browser support, privacy and recovery notes. | Browser-mediated install/update; safe prompt, manifest/icon/display requirements, rollback retains runnable cache. | Approved Android distribution/store channel; complete privacy/data-safety, signing, age/content, accessibility and release-note requirements before submission. | Approved App Store/TestFlight channel; complete privacy nutrition label, signing, age/content, accessibility and review requirements before submission. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-218-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-219-The shared game is capability-tested on current and previous agreed browser/OS\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-220-releases and representative phone, tablet and desktop classes. If an agreed\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-226-P0 observability is local and supportable: structured development/build logs,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-227-visible package/save/cache version status, and optional minimal local fault\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-228-record. Every fault must have player-facing recovery and evidence that save or\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md:229:cache protection held. External crash, analytics, account, commerce, live-op,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-230-multiplayer/moderation, notification, and sync providers remain optional and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-231-unintegrated until credentials, cost, data use, reliability and failure\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-232-behaviour receive approval.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md-235-| --- | --- |\nprojects/football-tri