non-alarming, non-looping, never replaces recovery choices. |\n+\n+## Playback and mixing policy\n+\n+Provide persistent per-local-profile master mute and independent music/feedback\n+controls. Honour platform/system volume, audio focus/interruption, and exposed\n+reduced-sensory preferences. Backgrounding pauses nonessential playback and\n+never affects game state. Do not autoplay audible music before player\n+interaction where platform policy requires it.\n+\n+The same IDs serve responsive web, PWA, Android, and iPhone. Web/PWA waits for\n+audio unlock and silently retains captions/text if unavailable; phones respect\n+mute switch/audio focus. Keyboard, touch, mouse, and gamepad invoke the same\n+semantic state and therefore the same cue. Remote/TV delivery is out of P0.\n+\n+Production tests cover speakers/headphones, system muted, audio unavailable,\n+screen-reader speech, interruption, offline cached assets, and reduced feedback.\n+Acceptance requires intended trigger once at safe state, correct loop/duration,\n+no required audio-only meaning, caption key, mute/volume support, permitted\n+source, and complete manifest provenance/checksum/review. Exact final rendered\n+count, loudness readings, formats, size budget, and language captions await\n+production approval; this plan creates or licenses no audio.\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5882d477494be9f0bd246763ec8d254f593d3d92\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@\n+# 04 \u2014 Experience contract\n+\n+**Traceability:** This contract implements the original *matchday knowledge* challenge in [01-creative-direction.md](01-creative-direction.md) and the first-release systems `GAME-001`\u2013`GAME-012` / journeys `J0`\u2013`J5` in [02-game-design-bible.md](02-game-design-bible.md) and [02-feature-model.md](02-feature-model.md). There is no narrative content model: this is a non-fiction trivia puzzle, whose arc is invitation, confident calls, rising momentum, decisive prompt, then clear celebration or explanation. It must not introduce campaign, battle, characters, or a fictional world.\n+\n+## Product promise and original language\n+\n+The player enters a calm abstract broadcast studio, chooses a compact themed knowledge round, answers one card at a time, and leaves knowing what happened and what was saved. The visual vocabulary is **category fields**, **signal sweeps**, **stat blocks**, **pitch-line geometry**, and **celebration shapes**: original abstract objects rather than a stadium, fixture, presenter, club, competition, or broadcaster. Prompt hierarchy is always question \u2192 answer action \u2192 explanation \u2192 score/streak. Category colour supports scanning but a written category label and a distinct pattern do the semantic work.\n+\n+Tone is precise, lively, adult, inclusive, and fact-first. Instructions use active plain language; correct feedback celebrates the decision, never the person; incorrect feedback explains without shaming. Questions, explanations, captions, error copy, and assets are independently authored. The Athletic and QuizUp establish only topic breadth and short-session outcomes: no marks, questions, wording, screen compositions, visual trade dress, audio, or interaction choreography may be reproduced.\n+\n+## Information architecture and navigation\n+\n+| Area / state | Purpose and primary actions | Navigation and recovery |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Home / local profile | Resume a confirmed paused run; begin `First Whistle`; choose a theme; open settings/help. | Home is the stable return target. Resume identifies the round and last confirmed boundary; a missing run simply omits Resume. |\n+| Round choice | Explain tutorial versus standard round, category, card count, timer mode, and availability. | Select starts only eligible validated content. An empty category says why and offers another eligible theme or Home. |\n+| Quiz / unresolved card | Show progress, question, format-specific answer control, optional pause, and accessible score/streak summary. | One card is actionable. Back/Pause opens a non-modal pause panel at a safe boundary; abandon requires confirmation. |\n+| Resolution / explanation | State correct/incorrect in text, icon, pattern, and optional cue; reveal canonical answer and concise explanation; continue only after state is clear. | Continue advances after a resolved snapshot boundary; no answer can be changed. |\n+| Results | Show answered/correct, score, best active-session streak, category, milestone/save status, then Replay, Choose theme, or Exit. | Reopening is read-only and never awards twice. |\n+| Settings / help | Text size, contrast, reduced motion, captions/descriptions, audio, input help, privacy/diagnostic choice, reset settings, and delete profile. | Available before or during a round; a changed setting takes effect immediately or at the next announced safe boundary. Return preserves the previous route. |\n+| Install/offline/update | Explain install readiness, cached-content state, download need, and a staged update. | Offline compatible content remains playable. Update applies only between rounds; decline/failed update retains the known-good package. |\n+| Recovery / error | Explain a write failure, corrupt draft, incompatible cache, or unexpected fault in plain language. | Offer only applicable Retry, Resume last confirmed state, Continue without saving, Discard draft, Return Home, or Reset cache after save protection. |\n+\n+No first-release account, multiplayer, chat, ranking, purchase, live event, or remote sync route exists. A future connected feature requires a separate identity, reporting, moderation, consent, retention, outage, and safety flow; it must not be implied by this IA.\n+\n+### State, privacy, and destructive-action rules\n+\n+- A disabled Submit names its condition; a typed blank needs a separate explicit \u201cSubmit blank\u201d choice.\n+- No eligible cards, unavailable first offline download, missing optional audio, unsupported gamepad, and unavailable language have explanatory fallback states, never a dead end or silent substitute.\n+- Failed saves keep the prior confirmed snapshot. Corrupt drafts offer the last confirmed snapshot or discard the draft; cache reset is never offered until save protection is reported.\n+- Abandon round, reset settings, and delete profile name their exact effects and offer Cancel as the initial safe action. Delete profile needs a final confirmation, removes local profile/settings/history/snapshots/recovery records/local diagnostics, and returns to first launch.\n+- Optional diagnostics and notifications are off until consent. Their panels state purpose, fields, retention/deletion, and any approved transport; denial never blocks play. P0 never requests names, contacts, location, ad/account IDs, payments, raw typed answers, question text, or save payloads.\n+\n+## Interaction contract by surface\n+\n+Semantic actions are `navigate`, `select`, `submit`, `back`, `pause`, `open-settings`, and `adjust-setting`. Every critical action has an equivalent on each available surface; presentation may adapt but rules/save semantics never do.\n+\n+| Surface | Layout and input choreography | Required adaptation |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Web desktop / laptop | Centered reading column with persistent top progress; pointer hover reveals only nonessential help. | Keyboard works without pointer: `Tab`/`Shift+Tab` follow reading order, Enter/Space activates, arrows move within a radio/ordered group, Escape/Back pauses or closes a non-destructive panel. Browser back never silently abandons a round. |\n+| Web phone / PWA / Android / iPhone | Portrait-first single column; question before answers; sticky but non-obscuring progress/pause row. Landscape is a reflow, not a required orientation. | All primary targets are at least 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px (or platform equivalent), separated to prevent accidental answer selection. No hover dependency; respects system text scaling and safe areas. |\n+| Gamepad | Same single-focus sequence as keyboard; focus lands on page title or first meaningful action after every route/state change. | D-pad/left stick navigates; primary face button selects/submits; secondary backs/closes; Menu/Start pauses. Unsupported/disconnected gamepad is explained while touch/keyboard remain available. |\n+| Mouse / trackpad | Pointer targets match visible controls; hover only supplements labels/tooltips. | Click has an equivalent keyboard action; focus remains visible after a click. |\n+| Screen reader, switch, voice, assistive input | Native semantic controls are preferred over canvas-only controls; actions have stable accessible names. | Voice can invoke visible unique labels such as \u201cSubmit answer\u201d and \u201cPause round\u201d; it need not parse football answers as commands. Switch uses the same finite focus order. Status changes announce once without stealing focus. |\n+\n+Remote-control/TV input is not a selected delivery target; it remains an approval item rather than implied P0 scope.\n+\n+## Responsive visual behaviour and tokens\n+\n+Use a portrait-first single-column core. At narrow widths, full-width answer controls stack. At tablet width, score/streak may sit beside the prompt only when reading measure and answer target size are preserved. At desktop width, cap the reading column; spare space is quiet studio texture, never a competing task. Reflow at browser zoom and system text enlargement; never truncate question, explanation, confirmation, or recovery copy.\n+\n+Tokens are semantic and product-specific: `FT-SPACE-1..6`, `FT-TYPE-PROMPT`, `FT-TYPE-BODY`, `FT-TYPE-NUMERIC`, `FT-SURFACE-BASE`, `FT-SURFACE-CATEGORY-{world,domestic,club,records}`, `FT-STATE-{focus,correct,incorrect,warning}`, `FT-PATTERN-{field,grid,sweep}`, and `FT-MOTION-{none,brief,celebrate}`. Normal text meets 4.5:1 (3:1 only for large text); essential icons, focus indicators, and control boundaries meet 3:1. High contrast uses tested semantic tokens, not saturation alone.\n+\n+Correct/incorrect combines a written result, icon, pattern/border, and optional audio. Focus is a high-contrast non-colour-only outline, never hidden behind sticky UI. Motion defaults to short non-flashing transitions; reduced motion replaces signal sweeps, card movement, and celebration bursts with immediate state changes. No animation flashes more than three times per second.\n+\n+## Accessibility and content requirements\n+\n+- Each route has one programmatic page title/heading and landmarks for header, main quiz, and complementary progress. Dialogs label their consequence, trap focus only while open, and restore focus to the invoker.\n+- Answer groups expose question text, format, selected state, position, and enabled/disabled reason. Score/streak labels are concise; progress exposes ordinal and total.\n+- Resolution uses a polite live region for outcome/score; blocking errors use assertive announcement only when action cannot continue. Captions/descriptions are visible on request and every cue has text. Decorative studio art is hidden from assistive tech.\n+- Text size persists and honours system scaling. Localisation externalises prompts, answers, explanations, categories, recovery/error strings, captions, and labels; a language is not selectable until aliases and factual review pass.\n+- Timer mode defaults off. If later enabled it states duration, has a non-timed alternative, offers extension/pause where applicable, and never prevents an explanation.\n+\n+## Journey-to-presentation map and acceptance\n+\n+| Journey | Location/screen state | Shared visual/audio IDs | Acceptance |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| J0 | Home, Settings, consent | `ASSET-SHL-001`, `ASSET-UI-001`, `AUDIO-SET-001` | Settings apply globally; consent denial remains playable; labels/focus order work. |\n+| J1 | First Whistle, prompt, resolution, results | `ASSET-QZ-001`, `ASSET-FBK-001..004`, `AUDIO-QZ-001..004` | Offline tutorial completes with readable non-colour feedback and confirmed save. |\n+| J2 | Theme choice, standard round, unavailable-theme empty state | `ASSET-QZ-002`, `AUDIO-QZ-001..003` | Eligible choice, clear empty state, replay/exit without social comparison. |\n+| J3 | Pause, save failure, recovery, delete confirmation | `ASSET-UI-003`, `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Prior confirmed state is protected; destructive choices are explicit/cancellable. |\n+| J4 | Editorial/release workflow, not player runtime | `ASSET-OPS-001` | Missing provenance or ambiguous answers block publish. |\n+| J5 | Download/update/error/recovery | `ASSET-SYS-001`, `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Safe-boundary update, offline fallback, retry/home, privacy-preserving diagnostic choice are clear. |\n+\n+Before release, verify each row with keyboard, touch, screen reader, system text enlargement, high contrast, reduced motion, muted audio/captions, offline cached content, failed save, corrupt draft, and deletion. Final browser/OS/device/performance matrix remains an approval gate in `03-technical-contract.md`.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --check -- projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md && rg -n 'ASSET-(SHL|QZ|UI|FBK|SYS|OPS|MKT)-|AUDIO-(MUS|QZ|RES|SET|SYS)-|J[0-5]|4\\\\.5:1|44 \u00d7 44' projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md:41:| `AUDIO-MUS-001` | Home/round-choice invitation bed; J0/J2 after screen settles. | Seamless 20\u201340 s loop with clean entry/exit. | Low-distraction music; mute/fade immediately; never masks UI feedback or speech. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md:42:| `AUDIO-QZ-001` | Prompt-ready tick; J1/J2 when an unresolved card is actionable. | One-shot \u22640.5 s. | Caption \u201cQuestion ready\u201d; visible/announced card is complete without it. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md:43:| `AUDIO-QZ-002` | Correct confirmation; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot \u22640.8 s. | Caption \u201cCorrect cue\u201d; distinguishable from incorrect without pitch alone; never precedes written result. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md:44:| `AUDIO-QZ-003` | Incorrect correction; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot \u22640.8 s. | Caption \u201cAnswer correction cue\u201d; calm/non-punitive; explanation remains primary. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md:45:| `AUDIO-QZ-004` | Streak threshold rise; J1/J2 on confirmed 3+ streak. | One-shot \u22641.2 s. | Caption \u201cStreak rises\u201d; one per card; suppressible under reduced feedback. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md:46:| `AUDIO-RES-001` | Results sting; J1/J2 when results first appear. | One-shot 2\u20134 s, never loops. | Caption \u201cRound complete\u201d; controls available immediately and meaningful muted. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md:47:| `AUDIO-SET-001` | Player-requested settings preview; J0 after audio preference change. | One-shot \u22640.5 s. | Obeys current volume/mute; visible labelled test control; never autoplays on Settings open. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md:48:| `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Package update ready/applied; J5 at a between-round state only. | One-shot \u22640.7 s. | Caption \u201cUpdate ready/applied\u201d; visible keyboard-accessible status/action. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md:49:| `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Save/recovery attention; J3 when recovery panel appears. | One-shot \u22640.7 s. | Caption \u201cSave attention cue\u201d; non-alarming, non-looping, never replaces recovery choices. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:28:`ASSET-FBK-001-correct-2x`); locale is a manifest field, not baked into a\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:45:| `ASSET-SHL-001` / P0 | App mark and quiet studio background: Home, install, results. | light/dark/high-contrast; phone/tablet/desktop crops; static. | Mark has an accessible name; background is decorative and preserves text/control contrast and safe areas. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:46:| `ASSET-QZ-001` / P0 | Reusable prompt-card field: First Whistle and standard question. | four category tokens; narrow/wide; no-text base. | Texture has no semantic meaning; prompt remains live scalable text. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:47:| `ASSET-QZ-002` / P0 | Category/round tile: choice and unavailable theme. | world/domestic/club/records; available/unavailable/selected/focus. | Label plus pattern distinguishes category; unavailable has explicit text and 3:1 boundaries. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:48:| `ASSET-UI-001` / P0 | Icons for pause, settings, resume, back, audio, captions, install. | default/focus/disabled/high-contrast; vector/1x/2x. | Icons supplement labels or have exact accessible names; non-colour focus and 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px target. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:49:| `ASSET-UI-003` / P0 | Pause, confirmation, recovery-panel framing. | normal/high-contrast/reduced-motion; modal/non-modal. | No essential text baked in; frame cannot cover focused action. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:50:| `ASSET-FBK-001` / P0 | Correct motif: rising signal/check and score increment. | correct/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Written \u201cCorrect\u201d, answer, and icon/pattern remain if art/motion/audio is absent. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:51:| `ASSET-FBK-002` / P0 | Incorrect motif: calm correction marker/explanation lead-in. | incorrect/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Never punitive; written outcome/explanation are primary. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:52:| `ASSET-FBK-003` / P0 | Streak stat block/celebration shape. | streak-3/streak-4-plus/static/reduced-motion. | Score/streak is text; no flash above three per second. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:53:| `ASSET-FBK-004` / P0 | Completion/result celebration shape. | complete/replay/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Results remain understandable without it; it cannot cover actions. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:54:| `ASSET-SYS-001` / P0 | Offline, update, cached-package, and error symbols. | ready/offline/downloading/failed/recovery. | Icon, text, and pattern pair; semantic UI announces errors. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:55:| `ASSET-OPS-001` / P1 | Internal editorial provenance/validation glyphs; J4 only. | draft/reviewed/blocked/published/withdrawn. | Text status is mandatory; icons cannot grant publication eligibility. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md:56:| `ASSET-MKT-001` / P1 | Store/PWA listing imagery from studio system. | platform ratios; accessible preview copy; no-text master. | Shows actual capabilities, original art, approved alt copy; not needed to play. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md:3:**Traceability:** This contract implements the original *matchday knowledge* challenge in [01-creative-direction.md](01-creative-direction.md) and the first-release systems `GAME-001`\u2013`GAME-012` / journeys `J0`\u2013`J5` in [02-game-design-bible.md](02-game-design-bible.md) and [02-feature-model.md](02-feature-model.md). There is no narrative content model: this is a non-fiction trivia puzzle, whose arc is invitation, confident calls, rising momentum, decisive prompt, then clear celebration or explanation. It must not introduce campaign, battle, characters, or a fictional world.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md:41:| Web phone / PWA / Android / iPhone | Portrait-first single column; question before answers; sticky but non-obscuring progress/pause row. Landscape is a reflow, not a required orientation. | All primary targets are at least 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px (or platform equivalent), separated to prevent accidental answer selection. No hover dependency; respects system text scaling and safe areas. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md:52:Tokens are semantic and product-specific: `FT-SPACE-1..6`, `FT-TYPE-PROMPT`, `FT-TYPE-BODY`, `FT-TYPE-NUMERIC`, `FT-SURFACE-BASE`, `FT-SURFACE-CATEGORY-{world,domestic,club,records}`, `FT-STATE-{focus,correct,incorrect,warning}`, `FT-PATTERN-{field,grid,sweep}`, and `FT-MOTION-{none,brief,celebrate}`. Normal text meets 4.5:1 (3:1 only for large text); essential icons, focus indicators, and control boundaries meet 3:1. High contrast uses tested semantic tokens, not saturation alone.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md:68:| J0 | Home, Settings, consent | `ASSET-SHL-001`, `ASSET-UI-001`, `AUDIO-SET-001` | Settings apply globally; consent denial remains playable; labels/focus order work. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md:69:| J1 | First Whistle, prompt, resolution, results | `ASSET-QZ-001`, `ASSET-FBK-001..004`, `AUDIO-QZ-001..004` | Offline tutorial completes with readable non-colour feedback and confirmed save. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md:70:| J2 | Theme choice, standard round, unavailable-theme empty state | `ASSET-QZ-002`, `AUDIO-QZ-001..003` | Eligible choice, clear empty state, replay/exit without social comparison. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md:71:| J3 | Pause, save failure, recovery, delete confirmation | `ASSET-UI-003`, `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Prior confirmed state is protected; destructive choices are explicit/cancellable. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md:72:| J4 | Editorial/release workflow, not player runtime | `ASSET-OPS-001` | Missing provenance or ambiguous answers block publish. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md:73:| J5 | Download/update/error/recovery | `ASSET-SYS-001`, `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Safe-boundary update, offline fallback, retry/home, privacy-preserving diagnostic choice are clear. |\n\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\nindex c5f7328dcf4019f6ded1b7ab82cb9ab117f427a8..7d933b5463fed33b86da324b92b93b2b428d6ab0\n--- a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\n@@ -13,3 +13,52 @@\n Asset quantities, file formats, and final delivery budgets remain pending target\n and packaging decisions. Each asset requires provenance and human creative\n review before production use.\n+\n+## Original-asset contract\n+\n+The asset language is the same original *matchday knowledge* studio described\n+in `01-creative-direction.md` and `04-experience-contract.md`: category fields,\n+pitch-line geometry, stat blocks, signal sweeps, and celebration shapes. It\n+must not become a stadium, club, competition, broadcaster, player, kit, crest,\n+or reference-product trade dress. This non-fiction trivia release has no\n+fictional characters, locations, dialogue portraits, maps, or gameplay worlds.\n+\n+IDs use `ASSET-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable once a package references\n+them. Variants append `-<state>-<size>` (for example,\n+`ASSET-FBK-001-correct-2x`); locale is a manifest field, not baked into a\n+universal visual. The asset manifest records ID, version, source/checksum,\n+owner, licence/provenance, alt-text/meaning, variants, and review status.\n+\n+Every release asset is created for this project or has documented rights. Do\n+not trace, scrape, prompt for, or modify a reference screenshot, mark, kit,\n+photo, or distinctive layout. Generated output retains prompt/model/version\n+and gets human originality review; third-party material needs licence and\n+attribution review. Uncertain provenance, embedded unlocalisable essential\n+text, missing alt/meaning treatment, or failed contrast/state review rejects\n+the asset. Decorative absence may fall back gracefully; required UI/state\n+assets reject a release.\n+\n+## Families, variants, and acceptance\n+\n+| Stable ID / priority | Purpose and screens | Required variants | Accessibility / acceptance |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `ASSET-SHL-001` / P0 | App mark and quiet studio background: Home, install, results. | light/dark/high-contrast; phone/tablet/desktop crops; static. | Mark has an accessible name; background is decorative and preserves text/control contrast and safe areas. |\n+| `ASSET-QZ-001` / P0 | Reusable prompt-card field: First Whistle and standard question. | four category tokens; narrow/wide; no-text base. | Texture has no semantic meaning; prompt remains live scalable text. |\n+| `ASSET-QZ-002` / P0 | Category/round tile: choice and unavailable theme. | world/domestic/club/records; available/unavailable/selected/focus. | Label plus pattern distinguishes category; unavailable has explicit text and 3:1 boundaries. |\n+| `ASSET-UI-001` / P0 | Icons for pause, settings, resume, back, audio, captions, install. | default/focus/disabled/high-contrast; vector/1x/2x. | Icons supplement labels or have exact accessible names; non-colour focus and 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px target. |\n+| `ASSET-UI-003` / P0 | Pause, confirmation, recovery-panel framing. | normal/high-contrast/reduced-motion; modal/non-modal. | No essential text baked in; frame cannot cover focused action. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-001` / P0 | Correct motif: rising signal/check and score increment. | correct/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Written \u201cCorrect\u201d, answer, and icon/pattern remain if art/motion/audio is absent. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-002` / P0 | Incorrect motif: calm correction marker/explanation lead-in. | incorrect/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Never punitive; written outcome/explanation are primary. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-003` / P0 | Streak stat block/celebration shape. | streak-3/streak-4-plus/static/reduced-motion. | Score/streak is text; no flash above three per second. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-004` / P0 | Completion/result celebration shape. | complete/replay/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Results remain understandable without it; it cannot cover actions. |\n+| `ASSET-SYS-001` / P0 | Offline, update, cached-package, and error symbols. | ready/offline/downloading/failed/recovery. | Icon, text, and pattern pair; semantic UI announces errors. |\n+| `ASSET-OPS-001` / P1 | Internal editorial provenance/validation glyphs; J4 only. | draft/reviewed/blocked/published/withdrawn. | Text status is mandatory; icons cannot grant publication eligibility. |\n+| `ASSET-MKT-001` / P1 | Store/PWA listing imagery from studio system. | platform ratios; accessible preview copy; no-text master. | Shows actual capabilities, original art, approved alt copy; not needed to play. |\n+\n+P0 sequence is shell \u2192 prompt/answer clarity \u2192 feedback/recovery \u2192 responsive\n+variants. No environment tiles, characters, portraits, item icons, effects\n+library, world map, or unrelated game-art family is in scope. For every ID,\n+review at 200% zoom, phone portrait, tablet, desktop, high contrast, reduced\n+motion, and with images disabled; verify mapping, non-colour state, label/alt,\n+safe crop, crispness, provenance/checksum, and no essential text burned into\n+reusable art. Final formats, byte budgets, and store specs await target approval.\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\nindex 80b9199a22884f3ba1a05ef471920526a4e70852..5c9fe5d73c333b34b7a0945f8daa5cae12b06a80\n--- a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\n@@ -12,3 +12,59 @@\n \n Final durations, quantities, loudness targets, loop policy, and generated-cue\n selection need production approval; no audio is generated by this plan.\n+\n+## Original-audio contract and cue IDs\n+\n+Audio reinforces the original *matchday knowledge* arc: invitation, confident\n+answer, rising streak, decisive result, and clear return. It shares the abstract\n+broadcast-studio vocabulary of `01-creative-direction.md` and the journey map\n+in `04-experience-contract.md`: bright electronic percussion, soft claps, warm\n+brass-like synth accents, and abstract crowd-energy texture. It is not a real\n+crowd, chant, anthem, commentary, broadcaster ident, club sound, football-game\n+imitation, or vocal performance associated with a real team.\n+\n+Cue IDs use `AUDIO-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable after package reference.\n+Rendered variants append `-<state>-<mix>`; a manifest records ID, source-session\n+or render checksum, creator/provenance, licence, loop points, loudness/peak,\n+duration, caption/description key, trigger, mix group, and review state.\n+Essential state also has text, icon/pattern, and semantic announcement. Captions\n+describe function (for example, \u201cbrief rising streak cue\u201d); missing audio never\n+blocks an action.\n+\n+P0 is instrumental only: no intelligible vocals, sampled speech, commentary,\n+chants, crowd recordings, or copyrighted musical imitation. Original/properly\n+licensed sources only; generated cues retain settings and receive human\n+originality review.\n+\n+| Stable ID | Purpose, journey, and trigger | Target loop / duration | Acceptance and accessibility |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `AUDIO-MUS-001` | Home/round-choice invitation bed; J0/J2 after screen settles. | Seamless 20\u201340 s loop with clean entry/exit. | Low-distraction music; mute/fade immediately; never masks UI feedback or speech. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-001` | Prompt-ready tick; J1/J2 when an unresolved card is actionable. | One-shot \u22640.5 s. | Caption \u201cQuestion ready\u201d; visible/announced card is complete without it. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-002` | Correct confirmation; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot \u22640.8 s. | Caption \u201cCorrect cue\u201d; distinguishable from incorrect without pitch alone; never precedes written result. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-003` | Incorrect correction; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot \u22640.8 s. | Caption \u201cAnswer correction cue\u201d; calm/non-punitive; explanation remains primary. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-004` | Streak threshold rise; J1/J2 on confirmed 3+ streak. | One-shot \u22641.2 s. | Caption \u201cStreak rises\u201d; one per card; suppressible under reduced feedback. |\n+| `AUDIO-RES-001` | Results sting; J1/J2 when results first appear. | One-shot 2\u20134 s, never loops. | Caption \u201cRound complete\u201d; controls available immediately and meaningful muted. |\n+| `AUDIO-SET-001` | Player-requested settings preview; J0 after audio preference change. | One-shot \u22640.5 s. | Obeys current volume/mute; visible labelled test control; never autoplays on Settings open. |\n+| `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Package update ready/applied; J5 at a between-round state only. | One-shot \u22640.7 s. | Caption \u201cUpdate ready/applied\u201d; visible keyboard-accessible status/action. |\n+| `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Save/recovery attention; J3 when recovery panel appears. | One-shot \u22640.7 s. | Caption \u201cSave attention cue\u201d; non-alarming, non-looping, never replaces recovery choices. |\n+\n+## Playback and mixing policy\n+\n+Provide persistent per-local-profile master mute and independent music/feedback\n+controls. Honour platform/system volume, audio focus/interruption, and exposed\n+reduced-sensory preferences. Backgrounding pauses nonessential playback and\n+never affects game state. Do not autoplay audible music before player\n+interaction where platform policy requires it.\n+\n+The same IDs serve responsive web, PWA, Android, and iPhone. Web/PWA waits for\n+audio unlock and silently retains captions/text if unavailable; phones respect\n+mute switch/audio focus. Keyboard, touch, mouse, and gamepad invoke the same\n+semantic state and therefore the same cue. Remote/TV delivery is out of P0.\n+\n+Production tests cover speakers/headphones, system muted, audio unavailable,\n+screen-reader speech, interruption, offline cached assets, and reduced feedback.\n+Acceptance requires intended trigger once at safe state, correct loop/duration,\n+no required audio-only meaning, caption key, mute/volume support, permitted\n+source, and complete manifest provenance/checksum/review. Exact final rendered\n+count, loudness readings, formats, size budget, and language captions await\n+production approval; this plan creates or licenses no audio.\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5882d477494be9f0bd246763ec8d254f593d3d92\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@\n+# 04 \u2014 Experience contract\n+\n+**Traceability:** This contract implements the original *matchday knowledge* challenge in [01-creative-direction.md](01-creative-direction.md) and the first-release systems `GAME-001`\u2013`GAME-012` / journeys `J0`\u2013`J5` in [02-game-design-bible.md](02-game-design-bible.md) and [02-feature-model.md](02-feature-model.md). There is no narrative content model: this is a non-fiction trivia puzzle, whose arc is invitation, confident calls, rising momentum, decisive prompt, then clear celebration or explanation. It must not introduce campaign, battle, characters, or a fictional world.\n+\n+## Product promise and original language\n+\n+The player enters a calm abstract broadcast studio, chooses a compact themed knowledge round, answers one card at a time, and leaves knowing what happened and what was saved. The visual vocabulary is **category fields**, **signal sweeps**, **stat blocks**, **pitch-line geometry**, and **celebration shapes**: original abstract objects rather than a stadium, fixture, presenter, club, competition, or broadcaster. Prompt hierarchy is always question \u2192 answer action \u2192 explanation \u2192 score/streak. Category colour supports scanning but a written category label and a distinct pattern do the semantic work.\n+\n+Tone is precise, lively, adult, inclusive, and fact-first. Instructions use active plain language; correct feedback celebrates the decision, never the person; incorrect feedback explains without shaming. Questions, explanations, captions, error copy, and assets are independently authored. The Athletic and QuizUp establish only topic breadth and short-session outcomes: no marks, questions, wording, screen compositions, visual trade dress, audio, or interaction choreography may be reproduced.\n+\n+## Information architecture and navigation\n+\n+| Area / state | Purpose and primary actions | Navigation and recovery |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Home / local profile | Resume a confirmed paused run; begin `First Whistle`; choose a theme; open settings/help. | Home is the stable return target. Resume identifies the round and last confirmed boundary; a missing run simply omits Resume. |\n+| Round choice | Explain tutorial versus standard round, category, card count, timer mode, and availability. | Select starts only eligible validated content. An empty category says why and offers another eligible theme or Home. |\n+| Quiz / unresolved card | Show progress, question, format-specific answer control, optional pause, and accessible score/streak summary. | One card is actionable. Back/Pause opens a non-modal pause panel at a safe boundary; abandon requires confirmation. |\n+| Resolution / explanation | State correct/incorrect in text, icon, pattern, and optional cue; reveal canonical answer and concise explanation; continue only after state is clear. | Continue advances after a resolved snapshot boundary; no answer can be changed. |\n+| Results | Show answered/correct, score, best active-session streak, category, milestone/save status, then Replay, Choose theme, or Exit. | Reopening is read-only and never awards twice. |\n+| Settings / help | Text size, contrast, reduced motion, captions/descriptions, audio, input help, privacy/diagnostic choice, reset settings, and delete profile. | Available before or during a round; a changed setting takes effect immediately or at the next announced safe boundary. Return preserves the previous route. |\n+| Install/offline/update | Explain install readiness, cached-content state, download need, and a staged update. | Offline compatible content remains playable. Update applies only between rounds; decline/failed update retains the known-good package. |\n+| Recovery / error | Explain a write failure, corrupt draft, incompatible cache, or unexpected fault in plain language. | Offer only applicable Retry, Resume last confirmed state, Continue without saving, Discard draft, Return Home, or Reset cache after save protection. |\n+\n+No first-release account, multiplayer, chat, ranking, purchase, live event, or remote sync route exists. A future connected feature requires a separate identity, reporting, moderation, consent, retention, outage, and safety flow; it must not be implied by this IA.\n+\n+### State, privacy, and destructive-action rules\n+\n+- A disabled Submit names its condition; a typed blank needs a separate explicit \u201cSubmit blank\u201d choice.\n+- No eligible cards, unavailable first offline download, missing optional audio, unsupported gamepad, and unavailable language have explanatory fallback states, never a dead end or silent substitute.\n+- Failed saves keep the prior confirmed snapshot. Corrupt drafts offer the last confirmed snapshot or discard the draft; cache reset is never offered until save protection is reported.\n+- Abandon round, reset settings, and delete profile name their exact effects and offer Cancel as the initial safe action. Delete profile needs a final confirmation, removes local profile/settings/history/snapshots/recovery records/local diagnostics, and returns to first launch.\n+- Optional diagnostics and notifications are off until consent. Their panels state purpose, fields, retention/deletion, and any approved transport; denial never blocks play. P0 never requests names, contacts, location, ad/account IDs, payments, raw typed answers, question text, or save payloads.\n+\n+## Interaction contract by surface\n+\n+Semantic actions are `navigate`, `select`, `submit`, `back`, `pause`, `open-settings`, and `adjust-setting`. Every critical action has an equivalent on each available surface; presentation may adapt but rules/save semantics never do.\n+\n+| Surface | Layout and input choreography | Required adaptation |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Web desktop / laptop | Centered reading column with persistent top progress; pointer hover reveals only nonessential help. | Keyboard works without pointer: `Tab`/`Shift+Tab` follow reading order, Enter/Space activates, arrows move within a radio/ordered group, Escape/Back pauses or closes a non-destructive panel. Browser back never silently abandons a round. |\n+| Web phone / PWA / Android / iPhone | Portrait-first single column; question before answers; sticky but non-obscuring progress/pause row. Landscape is a reflow, not a required orientation. | All primary targets are at least 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px (or platform equivalent), separated to prevent accidental answer selection. No hover dependency; respects system text scaling and safe areas. |\n+| Gamepad | Same single-focus sequence as keyboard; focus lands on page title or first meaningful action after every route/state change. | D-pad/left stick navigates; primary face button selects/submits; secondary backs/closes; Menu/Start pauses. Unsupported/disconnected gamepad is explained while touch/keyboard remain available. |\n+| Mouse / trackpad | Pointer targets match visible controls; hover only supplements labels/tooltips. | Click has an equivalent keyboard action; focus remains visible after a click. |\n+| Screen reader, switch, voice, assistive input | Native semantic controls are preferred over canvas-only controls; actions have stable accessible names. | Voice can invoke visible unique labels such as \u201cSubmit answer\u201d and \u201cPause round\u201d; it need not parse football answers as commands. Switch uses the same finite focus order. Status changes announce once without stealing focus. |\n+\n+Remote-control/TV input is not a selected delivery target; it remains an approval item rather than implied P0 scope.\n+\n+## Responsive visual behaviour and tokens\n+\n+Use a portrait-first single-column core. At narrow widths, full-width answer controls stack. At tablet width, score/streak may sit beside the prompt only when reading measure and answer target size are preserved. At desktop width, cap the reading column; spare space is quiet studio texture, never a competing task. Reflow at browser zoom and system text enlargement; never truncate question, explanation, confirmation, or recovery copy.\n+\n+Tokens are semantic and product-specific: `FT-SPACE-1..6`, `FT-TYPE-PROMPT`, `FT-TYPE-BODY`, `FT-TYPE-NUMERIC`, `FT-SURFACE-BASE`, `FT-SURFACE-CATEGORY-{world,domestic,club,records}`, `FT-STATE-{focus,correct,incorrect,warning}`, `FT-PATTERN-{field,grid,sweep}`, and `FT-MOTION-{none,brief,celebrate}`. Normal text meets 4.5:1 (3:1 only for large text); essential icons, focus indicators, and control boundaries meet 3:1. High contrast uses tested semantic tokens, not saturation alone.\n+\n+Correct/incorrect combines a written result, icon, pattern/border, and optional audio. Focus is a high-contrast non-colour-only outline, never hidden behind sticky UI. Motion defaults to short non-flashing transitions; reduced motion replaces signal sweeps, card movement, and celebration bursts with immediate state changes. No animation flashes more than three times per second.\n+\n+## Accessibility and content requirements\n+\n+- Each route has one programmatic page title/heading and landmarks for header, main quiz, and complementary progress. Dialogs label their consequence, trap focus only while open, and restore focus to the invoker.\n+- Answer groups expose question text, format, selected state, position, and enabled/disabled reason. Score/streak labels are concise; progress exposes ordinal and total.\n+- Resolution uses a polite live region for outcome/score; blocking errors use assertive announcement only when action cannot continue. Captions/descriptions are visible on request and every cue has text. Decorative studio art is hidden from assistive tech.\n+- Text size persists and honours system scaling. Localisation externalises prompts, answers, explanations, categories, recovery/error strings, captions, and labels; a language is not selectable until aliases and factual review pass.\n+- Timer mode defaults off. If later enabled it states duration, has a non-timed alternative, offers extension/pause where applicable, and never prevents an explanation.\n+\n+## Journey-to-presentation map and acceptance\n+\n+| Journey | Location/screen state | Shared visual/audio IDs | Acceptance |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| J0 | Home, Settings, consent | `ASSET-SHL-001`, `ASSET-UI-001`, `AUDIO-SET-001` | Settings apply globally; consent denial remains playable; labels/focus order work. |\n+| J1 | First Whistle, prompt, resolution, results | `ASSET-QZ-001`, `ASSET-FBK-001..004`, `AUDIO-QZ-001..004` | Offline tutorial completes with readable non-colour feedback and confirmed save. |\n+| J2 | Theme choice, standard round, unavailable-theme empty state | `ASSET-QZ-002`, `AUDIO-QZ-001..003` | Eligible choice, clear empty state, replay/exit without social comparison. |\n+| J3 | Pause, save failure, recovery, delete confirmation | `ASSET-UI-003`, `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Prior confirmed state is protected; destructive choices are explicit/cancellable. |\n+| J4 | Editorial/release workflow, not player runtime | `ASSET-OPS-001` | Missing provenance or ambiguous answers block publish. |\n+| J5 | Download/update/error/recovery | `ASSET-SYS-001`, `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Safe-boundary update, offline fallback, retry/home, privacy-preserving diagnostic choice are clear. |\n+\n+Before release, verify each row with keyboard, touch, screen reader, system text enlargement, high contrast, reduced motion, muted audio/captions, offline cached content, failed save, corrupt draft, and deletion. Final browser/OS/device/performance matrix remains an approval gate in `03-technical-contract.md`.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The three specification contracts are now in place: the experience document defines the original responsive interaction and accessibility model, while asset and audio plans now assign stable, journey-traceable IDs and acceptance rules.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\"],\"test_result\":\"`git diff --check -- <three specification files>` passed. A focused `rg` trace check confirmed asset/cue identifiers, J0\u2013J5 coverage, 44 \u00d7 44 px touch targets, and 4.5:1 contrast policy across the contracts.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Inspected the existing creative direction, game design bible, feature model, and technical contract. Codebase Memory architecture request was attempted first but cancelled by the MCP service; document-only discovery then used focused file listing and excerpts.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"git diff --check exited 0; focused trace search exited 0.\",\"browser_log\":\"Not applicable: documentation-only domain contract change.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"Navigation, empty/error states, feedback, destructive actions, and privacy-sensitive content are specified.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"04-experience-contract.md defines IA routes, fallback/error states, recovery, destructive confirmations, and diagnostic/privacy consent policy.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Tokens, keyboard behaviour, focus, screen-reader labels, contrast, touch targets, and reduced motion are defined.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Experience contract defines FT semantic tokens, keyboard/gamepad mappings, focus/live-region rules, 4.5:1 contrast, 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px targets, and reduced-motion substitution.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The proposed experience is original and does not reproduce a reference product's trade dress.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"All three contracts explicitly constrain the identity to original abstract broadcast-studio vocabulary and prohibit copying reference marks, layouts, copy, assets, and choreography.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Where visual assets are in scope, the asset plan assigns stable, product-specific asset-family IDs, purpose, variants, provenance/originality, accessibility, and acceptance requirements.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"04-asset-direction.md assigns ASSET-SHL/QZ/UI/FBK/SYS/OPS/MKT IDs with purpose, variants, provenance manifest, accessibility, priorities, and review requirements.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Where audio is in scope, the cue map assigns stable, product-specific cue IDs and purpose, loop/duration, interaction trigger, and acceptance requirements.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"04-audio-direction.md defines AUDIO-MUS/QZ/RES/SET/SYS IDs with trigger, loop/duration targets, captions, mixing, provenance, and acceptance.\"},{\"criterion\":\"For every game and narrative-led product, creative, narrative, visual, and audio documents share a traceable premise/tone/content vocabulary and map their first-release locations, characters, scenes, UI states, and cues to user/player journeys.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Experience contract traces the non-fiction game\u2019s matchday-knowledge premise and J0\u2013J5 states to ASSET/AUDIO IDs; asset/audio contracts share that vocabulary and explicitly record that fictional characters/locations/scenes are out of scope.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\"],\"summary\":\"Added the requested experience contract and expanded the existing game asset/audio direction documents. README was not changed because this is a project specification-stage change with no setup, command, or implemented behaviour change.\"},\"known_limitations\":[\"Final OS/browser/device support matrix, performance/download budgets, store requirements, final audio renders/loudness measurements, and language selection remain approval gates already recorded in the technical contract.\"],\"browser_coverage\":\"No Playwright specification changed because this is documentation-only domain-contract work with no browser implementation to exercise.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\nindex c5f7328dcf4019f6ded1b7ab82cb9ab117f427a8..7d933b5463fed33b86da324b92b93b2b428d6ab0\n--- a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\n@@ -13,3 +13,52 @@\n Asset quantities, file formats, and final delivery budgets remain pending target\n and packaging decisions. Each asset requires provenance and human creative\n review before production use.\n+\n+## Original-asset contract\n+\n+The asset language is the same original *matchday knowledge* studio described\n+in `01-creative-direction.md` and `04-experience-contract.md`: category fields,\n+pitch-line geometry, stat blocks, signal sweeps, and celebration shapes. It\n+must not become a stadium, club, competition, broadcaster, player, kit, crest,\n+or reference-product trade dress. This non-fiction trivia release has no\n+fictional characters, locations, dialogue portraits, maps, or gameplay worlds.\n+\n+IDs use `ASSET-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable once a package references\n+them. Variants append `-<state>-<size>` (for example,\n+`ASSET-FBK-001-correct-2x`); locale is a manifest field, not baked into a\n+universal visual. The asset manifest records ID, version, source/checksum,\n+owner, licence/provenance, alt-text/meaning, variants, and review status.\n+\n+Every release asset is created for this project or has documented rights. Do\n+not trace, scrape, prompt for, or modify a reference screenshot, mark, kit,\n+photo, or distinctive layout. Generated output retains prompt/model/version\n+and gets human originality review; third-party material needs licence and\n+attribution review. Uncertain provenance, embedded unlocalisable essential\n+text, missing alt/meaning treatment, or failed contrast/state review rejects\n+the asset. Decorative absence may fall back gracefully; required UI/state\n+assets reject a release.\n+\n+## Families, variants, and acceptance\n+\n+| Stable ID / priority | Purpose and screens | Required variants | Accessibility / acceptance |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `ASSET-SHL-001` / P0 | App mark and quiet studio background: Home, install, results. | light/dark/high-contrast; phone/tablet/desktop crops; static. | Mark has an accessible name; background is decorative and preserves text/control contrast and safe areas. |\n+| `ASSET-QZ-001` / P0 | Reusable prompt-card field: First Whistle and standard question. | four category tokens; narrow/wide; no-text base. | Texture has no semantic meaning; prompt remains live scalable text. |\n+| `ASSET-QZ-002` / P0 | Category/round tile: choice and unavailable theme. | world/domestic/club/records; available/unavailable/selected/focus. | Label plus pattern distinguishes category; unavailable has explicit text and 3:1 boundaries. |\n+| `ASSET-UI-001` / P0 | Icons for pause, settings, resume, back, audio, captions, install. | default/focus/disabled/high-contrast; vector/1x/2x. | Icons supplement labels or have exact accessible names; non-colour focus and 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px target. |\n+| `ASSET-UI-003` / P0 | Pause, confirmation, recovery-panel framing. | normal/high-contrast/reduced-motion; modal/non-modal. | No essential text baked in; frame cannot cover focused action. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-001` / P0 | Correct motif: rising signal/check and score increment. | correct/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Written \u201cCorrect\u201d, answer, and icon/pattern remain if art/motion/audio is absent. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-002` / P0 | Incorrect motif: calm correction marker/explanation lead-in. | incorrect/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Never punitive; written outcome/explanation are primary. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-003` / P0 | Streak stat block/celebration shape. | streak-3/streak-4-plus/static/reduced-motion. | Score/streak is text; no flash above three per second. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-004` / P0 | Completion/result celebration shape. | complete/replay/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Results remain understandable without it; it cannot cover actions. |\n+| `ASSET-SYS-001` / P0 | Offline, update, cached-package, and error symbols. | ready/offline/downloading/failed/recovery. | Icon, text, and pattern pair; semantic UI announces errors. |\n+| `ASSET-OPS-001` / P1 | Internal editorial provenance/validation glyphs; J4 only. | draft/reviewed/blocked/published/withdrawn. | Text status is mandatory; icons cannot grant publication eligibility. |\n+| `ASSET-MKT-001` / P1 | Store/PWA listing imagery from studio system. | platform ratios; accessible preview copy; no-text master. | Shows actual capabilities, original art, approved alt copy; not needed to play. |\n+\n+P0 sequence is shell \u2192 prompt/answer clarity \u2192 feedback/recovery \u2192 responsive\n+variants. No environment tiles, characters, portraits, item icons, effects\n+library, world map, or unrelated game-art family is in scope. For every ID,\n+review at 200% zoom, phone portrait, tablet, desktop, high contrast, reduced\n+motion, and with images disabled; verify mapping, non-colour state, label/alt,\n+safe crop, crispness, provenance/checksum, and no essential text burned into\n+reusable art. Final formats, byte budgets, and store specs await target approval.\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\nindex 80b9199a22884f3ba1a05ef471920526a4e70852..5c9fe5d73c333b34b7a0945f8daa5cae12b06a80\n--- a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\n@@ -12,3 +12,59 @@\n \n Final durations, quantities, loudness targets, loop policy, and generated-cue\n selection need production approval; no audio is generated by this plan.\n+\n+## Original-audio contract and cue IDs\n+\n+Audio reinforces the original *matchday knowledge* arc: invitation, confident\n+answer, rising streak, decisive result, and clear return. It shares the abstract\n+broadcast-studio vocabulary of `01-creative-direction.md` and the journey map\n+in `04-experience-contract.md`: bright electronic percussion, soft claps, warm\n+brass-like synth accents, and abstract crowd-energy texture. It is not a real\n+crowd, chant, anthem, commentary, broadcaster ident, club sound, football-game\n+imitation, or vocal performance associated with a real team.\n+\n+Cue IDs use `AUDIO-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable after package reference.\n+Rendered variants append `-<state>-<mix>`; a manifest records ID, source-session\n+or render checksum, creator/provenance, licence, loop points, loudness/peak,\n+duration, caption/description key, trigger, mix group, and review state.\n+Essential state also has text, icon/pattern, and semantic announcement. Captions\n+describe function (for example, \u201cbrief rising streak cue\u201d); missing audio never\n+blocks an action.\n+\n+P0 is instrumental only: no intelligible vocals, sampled speech, commentary,\n+chants, crowd recordings, or copyrighted musical imitation. Original/properly\n+licensed sources only; generated cues retain settings and receive human\n+originality review.\n+\n+| Stable ID | Purpose, journey, and trigger | Target loop / duration | Acceptance and accessibility |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `AUDIO-MUS-001` | Home/round-choice invitation bed; J0/J2 after screen settles. | Seamless 20\u201340 s loop with clean entry/exit. | Low-distraction music; mute/fade immediately; never masks UI feedback or speech. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-001` | Prompt-ready tick; J1/J2 when an unresolved card is actionable. | One-shot \u22640.5 s. | Caption \u201cQuestion ready\u201d; visible/announced card is complete without it. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-002` | Correct confirmation; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot \u22640.8 s. | Caption \u201cCorrect cue\u201d; distinguishable from incorrect without pitch alone; never precedes written result. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-003` | Incorrect correction; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot \u22640.8 s. | Caption \u201cAnswer correction cue\u201d; calm/non-punitive; explanation remains primary. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-004` | Streak threshold rise; J1/J2 on confirmed 3+ streak. | One-shot \u22641.2 s. | Caption \u201cStreak rises\u201d; one per card; suppressible under reduced feedback. |\n+| `AUDIO-RES-001` | Results sting; J1/J2 when results first appear. | One-shot 2\u20134 s, never loops. | Caption \u201cRound complete\u201d; controls available immediately and meaningful muted. |\n+| `AUDIO-SET-001` | Player-requested settings preview; J0 after audio preference change. | One-shot \u22640.5 s. | Obeys current volume/mute; visible labelled test control; never autoplays on Settings open. |\n+| `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Package update ready/applied; J5 at a between-round state only. | One-shot \u22640.7 s. | Caption \u201cUpdate ready/applied\u201d; visible keyboard-accessible status/action. |\n+| `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Save/recovery attention; J3 when recovery panel appears. | One-shot \u22640.7 s. | Caption \u201cSave attention cue\u201d; non-alarming, non-looping, never replaces recovery choices. |\n+\n+## Playback and mixing policy\n+\n+Provide persistent per-local-profile master mute and independent music/feedback\n+controls. Honour platform/system volume, audio focus/interruption, and exposed\n+reduced-sensory preferences. Backgrounding pauses nonessential playback and\n+never affects game state. Do not autoplay audible music before player\n+interaction where platform policy requires it.\n+\n+The same IDs serve responsive web, PWA, Android, and iPhone. Web/PWA waits for\n+audio unlock and silently retains captions/text if unavailable; phones respect\n+mute switch/audio focus. Keyboard, touch, mouse, and gamepad invoke the same\n+semantic state and therefore the same cue. Remote/TV delivery is out of P0.\n+\n+Production tests cover speakers/headphones, system muted, audio unavailable,\n+screen-reader speech, interruption, offline cached assets, and reduced feedback.\n+Acceptance requires intended trigger once at safe state, correct loop/duration,\n+no required audio-only meaning, caption key, mute/volume support, permitted\n+source, and complete manifest provenance/checksum/review. Exact final rendered\n+count, loudness readings, formats, size budget, and language captions await\n+production approval; this plan creates or licenses no audio.\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5882d477494be9f0bd246763ec8d254f593d3d92\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@\n+# 04 \u2014 Experience contract\n+\n+**Traceability:** This contract implements the original *matchday knowledge* challenge in [01-creative-direction.md](01-creative-direction.md) and the first-release systems `GAME-001`\u2013`GAME-012` / journeys `J0`\u2013`J5` in [02-game-design-bible.md](02-game-design-bible.md) and [02-feature-model.md](02-feature-model.md). There is no narrative content model: this is a non-fiction trivia puzzle, whose arc is invitation, confident calls, rising momentum, decisive prompt, then clear celebration or explanation. It must not introduce campaign, battle, characters, or a fictional world.\n+\n+## Product promise and original language\n+\n+The player enters a calm abstract broadcast studio, chooses a compact themed knowledge round, answers one card at a time, and leaves knowing what happened and what was saved. The visual vocabulary is **category fields**, **signal sweeps**, **stat blocks**, **pitch-line geometry**, and **celebration shapes**: original abstract objects rather than a stadium, fixture, presenter, club, competition, or broadcaster. Prompt hierarchy is always question \u2192 answer action \u2192 explanation \u2192 score/streak. Category colour supports scanning but a written category label and a distinct pattern do the semantic work.\n+\n+Tone is precise, lively, adult, inclusive, and fact-first. Instructions use active plain language; correct feedback celebrates the decision, never the person; incorrect feedback explains without shaming. Questions, explanations, captions, error copy, and assets are independently authored. The Athletic and QuizUp establish only topic breadth and short-session outcomes: no marks, questions, wording, screen compositions, visual trade dress, audio, or interaction choreography may be reproduced.\n+\n+## Information architecture and navigation\n+\n+| Area / state | Purpose and primary actions | Navigation and recovery |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Home / local profile | Resume a confirmed paused run; begin `First Whistle`; choose a theme; open settings/help. | Home is the stable return target. Resume identifies the round and last confirmed boundary; a missing run simply omits Resume. |\n+| Round choice | Explain tutorial versus standard round, category, card count, timer mode, and availability. | Select starts only eligible validated content. An empty category says why and offers another eligible theme or Home. |\n+| Quiz / unresolved card | Show progress, question, format-specific answer control, optional pause, and accessible score/streak summary. | One card is actionable. Back/Pause opens a non-modal pause panel at a safe boundary; abandon requires confirmation. |\n+| Resolution / explanation | State correct/incorrect in text, icon, pattern, and optional cue; reveal canonical answer and concise explanation; continue only after state is clear. | Continue advances after a resolved snapshot boundary; no answer can be changed. |\n+| Results | Show answered/correct, score, best active-session streak, category, milestone/save status, then Replay, Choose theme, or Exit. | Reopening is read-only and never awards twice. |\n+| Settings / help | Text size, contrast, reduced motion, captions/descriptions, audio, input help, privacy/diagnostic choice, reset settings, and delete profile. | Available before or during a round; a changed setting takes effect immediately or at the next announced safe boundary. Return preserves the previous route. |\n+| Install/offline/update | Explain install readiness, cached-content state, download need, and a staged update. | Offline compatible content remains playable. Update applies only between rounds; decline/failed update retains the known-good package. |\n+| Recovery / error | Explain a write failure, corrupt draft, incompatible cache, or unexpected fault in plain language. | Offer only applicable Retry, Resume last confirmed state, Continue without saving, Discard draft, Return Home, or Reset cache after save protection. |\n+\n+No first-release account, multiplayer, chat, ranking, purchase, live event, or remote sync route exists. A future connected feature requires a separate identity, reporting, moderation, consent, retention, outage, and safety flow; it must not be implied by this IA.\n+\n+### State, privacy, and destructive-action rules\n+\n+- A disabled Submit names its condition; a typed blank needs a separate explicit \u201cSubmit blank\u201d choice.\n+- No eligible cards, unavailable first offline download, missing optional audio, unsupported gamepad, and unavailable language have explanatory fallback states, never a dead end or silent substitute.\n+- Failed saves keep the prior confirmed snapshot. Corrupt drafts offer the last confirmed snapshot or discard the draft; cache reset is never offered until save protection is reported.\n+- Abandon round, reset settings, and delete profile name their exact effects and offer Cancel as the initial safe action. Delete profile needs a final confirmation, removes local profile/settings/history/snapshots/recovery records/local diagnostics, and returns to first launch.\n+- Optional diagnostics and notifications are off until consent. Their panels state purpose, fields, retention/deletion, and any approved transport; denial never blocks play. P0 never requests names, contacts, location, ad/account IDs, payments, raw typed answers, question text, or save payloads.\n+\n+## Interaction contract by surface\n+\n+Semantic actions are `navigate`, `select`, `submit`, `back`, `pause`, `open-settings`, and `adjust-setting`. Every critical action has an equivalent on each available surface; presentation may adapt but rules/save semantics never do.\n+\n+| Surface | Layout and input choreography | Required adaptation |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Web desktop / laptop | Centered reading column with persistent top progress; pointer hover reveals only nonessential help. | Keyboard works without pointer: `Tab`/`Shift+Tab` follow reading order, Enter/Space activates, arrows move within a radio/ordered group, Escape/Back pauses or closes a non-destructive panel. Browser back never silently abandons a round. |\n+| Web phone / PWA / Android / iPhone | Portrait-first single column; question before answers; sticky but non-obscuring progress/pause row. Landscape is a reflow, not a required orientation. | All primary targets are at least 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px (or platform equivalent), separated to prevent accidental answer selection. No hover dependency; respects system text scaling and safe areas. |\n+| Gamepad | Same single-focus sequence as keyboard; focus lands on page title or first meaningful action after every route/state change. | D-pad/left stick navigates; primary face button selects/submits; secondary backs/closes; Menu/Start pauses. Unsupported/disconnected gamepad is explained while touch/keyboard remain available. |\n+| Mouse / trackpad | Pointer targets match visible controls; hover only supplements labels/tooltips. | Click has an equivalent keyboard action; focus remains visible after a click. |\n+| Screen reader, switch, voice, assistive input | Native semantic controls are preferred over canvas-only controls; actions have stable accessible names. | Voice can invoke visible unique labels such as \u201cSubmit answer\u201d and \u201cPause round\u201d; it need not parse football answers as commands. Switch uses the same finite focus order. Status changes announce once without stealing focus. |\n+\n+Remote-control/TV input is not a selected delivery target; it remains an approval item rather than implied P0 scope.\n+\n+## Responsive visual behaviour and tokens\n+\n+Use a portrait-first single-column core. At narrow widths, full-width answer controls stack. At tablet width, score/streak may sit beside the prompt only when reading measure and answer target size are preserved. At desktop width, cap the reading column; spare space is quiet studio texture, never a competing task. Reflow at browser zoom and system text enlargement; never truncate question, explanation, confirmation, or recovery copy.\n+\n+Tokens are semantic and product-specific: `FT-SPACE-1..6`, `FT-TYPE-PROMPT`, `FT-TYPE-BODY`, `FT-TYPE-NUMERIC`, `FT-SURFACE-BASE`, `FT-SURFACE-CATEGORY-{world,domestic,club,records}`, `FT-STATE-{focus,correct,incorrect,warning}`, `FT-PATTERN-{field,grid,sweep}`, and `FT-MOTION-{none,brief,celebrate}`. Normal text meets 4.5:1 (3:1 only for large text); essential icons, focus indicators, and control boundaries meet 3:1. High contrast uses tested semantic tokens, not saturation alone.\n+\n+Correct/incorrect combines a written result, icon, pattern/border, and optional audio. Focus is a high-contrast non-colour-only outline, never hidden behind sticky UI. Motion defaults to short non-flashing transitions; reduced motion replaces signal sweeps, card movement, and celebration bursts with immediate state changes. No animation flashes more than three times per second.\n+\n+## Accessibility and content requirements\n+\n+- Each route has one programmatic page title/heading and landmarks for header, main quiz, and complementary progress. Dialogs label their consequence, trap focus only while open, and restore focus to the invoker.\n+- Answer groups expose question text, format, selected state, position, and enabled/disabled reason. Score/streak labels are concise; progress exposes ordinal and total.\n+- Resolution uses a polite live region for outcome/score; blocking errors use assertive announcement only when action cannot continue. Captions/descriptions are visible on request and every cue has text. Decorative studio art is hidden from assistive tech.\n+- Text size persists and honours system scaling. Localisation externalises prompts, answers, explanations, categories, recovery/error strings, captions, and labels; a language is not selectable until aliases and factual review pass.\n+- Timer mode defaults off. If later enabled it states duration, has a non-timed alternative, offers extension/pause where applicable, and never prevents an explanation.\n+\n+## Journey-to-presentation map and acceptance\n+\n+| Journey | Location/screen state | Shared visual/audio IDs | Acceptance |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| J0 | Home, Settings, consent | `ASSET-SHL-001`, `ASSET-UI-001`, `AUDIO-SET-001` | Settings apply globally; consent denial remains playable; labels/focus order work. |\n+| J1 | First Whistle, prompt, resolution, results | `ASSET-QZ-001`, `ASSET-FBK-001..004`, `AUDIO-QZ-001..004` | Offline tutorial completes with readable non-colour feedback and confirmed save. |\n+| J2 | Theme choice, standard round, unavailable-theme empty state | `ASSET-QZ-002`, `AUDIO-QZ-001..003` | Eligible choice, clear empty state, replay/exit without social comparison. |\n+| J3 | Pause, save failure, recovery, delete confirmation | `ASSET-UI-003`, `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Prior confirmed state is protected; destructive choices are explicit/cancellable. |\n+| J4 | Editorial/release workflow, not player runtime | `ASSET-OPS-001` | Missing provenance or ambiguous answers block publish. |\n+| J5 | Download/update/error/recovery | `ASSET-SYS-001`, `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Safe-boundary update, offline fallback, retry/home, privacy-preserving diagnostic choice are clear. |\n+\n+Before release, verify each row with keyboard, touch, screen reader, system text enlargement, high contrast, reduced motion, muted audio/captions, offline cached content, failed save, corrupt draft, and deletion. Final browser/OS/device/performance matrix remains an approval gate in `03-technical-contract.md`.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Created the original experience contract and expanded game asset/audio direction with traceable IDs, accessibility policy, and journey coverage.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\"],\"test_result\":\"Passed: `git diff --check -- projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md`. Passed focused `rg` trace check for journey IDs, asset/cue IDs, touch targets, and contrast policy.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Reviewed creative direction, game design bible, feature model, and technical contract. Codebase Memory architecture call was attempted first but cancelled by the MCP service; focused documentation inspection was used.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"Diff whitespace and identifier trace checks exited successfully.\",\"browser_log\":\"Not applicable: documentation-only change.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"Navigation, empty/error states, feedback, destructive actions, and privacy-sensitive content are specified.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Experience contract defines IA, fallback/error and recovery states, feedback, destructive confirmations, and diagnostic/privacy consent.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Tokens, keyboard behaviour, focus, screen-reader labels, contrast, touch targets, and reduced motion are defined.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Defines semantic tokens, keyboard/gamepad mappings, focus/live-region rules, 4.5:1 contrast, 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px targets, and reduced-motion behaviour.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The proposed experience is original and does not reproduce a reference product's trade dress.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Contracts require an original abstract broadcast-studio identity and prohibit copied marks, layouts, copy, assets, and choreography.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Where visual assets are in scope, the asset plan assigns stable, product-specific asset-family IDs, purpose, variants, provenance/originality, accessibility, and acceptance requirements.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Asset direction assigns ASSET-SHL/QZ/UI/FBK/SYS/OPS/MKT IDs with variants, provenance, accessibility, priority, and review rules.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Where audio is in scope, the cue map assigns stable, product-specific cue IDs and purpose, loop/duration, interaction trigger, and acceptance requirements.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Audio direction defines AUDIO-MUS/QZ/RES/SET/SYS IDs with triggers, duration/loop targets, captions, mixing, provenance, and acceptance.\"},{\"criterion\":\"For every game and narrative-led product, creative, narrative, visual, and audio documents share a traceable premise/tone/content vocabulary and map their first-release locations, characters, scenes, UI states, and cues to user/player journeys.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"The experience contract maps the non-fiction matchday-knowledge premise and J0\u2013J5 UI states to asset/audio IDs; asset/audio documents share that vocabulary and explicitly exclude fictional scenes/characters.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\"],\"summary\":\"Added the requested experience contract and expanded existing asset/audio direction. README was not changed because no setup, command, architecture, or implemented product behaviour changed.\"},\"known_limitations\":[\"Final support matrix, performance/download budgets, store requirements, rendered audio/loudness measurements, and language selection remain existing approval gates.\"],\"browser_coverage\":\"No Playwright spec changed because this is documentation-only domain-contract work without browser implementation.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\nindex c5f7328dcf4019f6ded1b7ab82cb9ab117f427a8..7d933b5463fed33b86da324b92b93b2b428d6ab0\n--- a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\n@@ -13,3 +13,52 @@\n Asset quantities, file formats, and final delivery budgets remain pending target\n and packaging decisions. Each asset requires provenance and human creative\n review before production use.\n+\n+## Original-asset contract\n+\n+The asset language is the same original *matchday knowledge* studio described\n+in `01-creative-direction.md` and `04-experience-contract.md`: category fields,\n+pitch-line geometry, stat blocks, signal sweeps, and celebration shapes. It\n+must not become a stadium, club, competition, broadcaster, player, kit, crest,\n+or reference-product trade dress. This non-fiction trivia release has no\n+fictional characters, locations, dialogue portraits, maps, or gameplay worlds.\n+\n+IDs use `ASSET-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable once a package references\n+them. Variants append `-<state>-<size>` (for example,\n+`ASSET-FBK-001-correct-2x`); locale is a manifest field, not baked into a\n+universal visual. The asset manifest records ID, version, source/checksum,\n+owner, licence/provenance, alt-text/meaning, variants, and review status.\n+\n+Every release asset is created for this project or has documented rights. Do\n+not trace, scrape, prompt for, or modify a reference screenshot, mark, kit,\n+photo, or distinctive layout. Generated output retains prompt/model/version\n+and gets human originality review; third-party material needs licence and\n+attribution review. Uncertain provenance, embedded unlocalisable essential\n+text, missing alt/meaning treatment, or failed contrast/state review rejects\n+the asset. Decorative absence may fall back gracefully; required UI/state\n+assets reject a release.\n+\n+## Families, variants, and acceptance\n+\n+| Stable ID / priority | Purpose and screens | Required variants | Accessibility / acceptance |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `ASSET-SHL-001` / P0 | App mark and quiet studio background: Home, install, results. | light/dark/high-contrast; phone/tablet/desktop crops; static. | Mark has an accessible name; background is decorative and preserves text/control contrast and safe areas. |\n+| `ASSET-QZ-001` / P0 | Reusable prompt-card field: First Whistle and standard question. | four category tokens; narrow/wide; no-text base. | Texture has no semantic meaning; prompt remains live scalable text. |\n+| `ASSET-QZ-002` / P0 | Category/round tile: choice and unavailable theme. | world/domestic/club/records; available/unavailable/selected/focus. | Label plus pattern distinguishes category; unavailable has explicit text and 3:1 boundaries. |\n+| `ASSET-UI-001` / P0 | Icons for pause, settings, resume, back, audio, captions, install. | default/focus/disabled/high-contrast; vector/1x/2x. | Icons supplement labels or have exact accessible names; non-colour focus and 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px target. |\n+| `ASSET-UI-003` / P0 | Pause, confirmation, recovery-panel framing. | normal/high-contrast/reduced-motion; modal/non-modal. | No essential text baked in; frame cannot cover focused action. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-001` / P0 | Correct motif: rising signal/check and score increment. | correct/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Written \u201cCorrect\u201d, answer, and icon/pattern remain if art/motion/audio is absent. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-002` / P0 | Incorrect motif: calm correction marker/explanation lead-in. | incorrect/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Never punitive; written outcome/explanation are primary. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-003` / P0 | Streak stat block/celebration shape. | streak-3/streak-4-plus/static/reduced-motion. | Score/streak is text; no flash above three per second. |\n+| `ASSET-FBK-004` / P0 | Completion/result celebration shape. | complete/replay/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Results remain understandable without it; it cannot cover actions. |\n+| `ASSET-SYS-001` / P0 | Offline, update, cached-package, and error symbols. | ready/offline/downloading/failed/recovery. | Icon, text, and pattern pair; semantic UI announces errors. |\n+| `ASSET-OPS-001` / P1 | Internal editorial provenance/validation glyphs; J4 only. | draft/reviewed/blocked/published/withdrawn. | Text status is mandatory; icons cannot grant publication eligibility. |\n+| `ASSET-MKT-001` / P1 | Store/PWA listing imagery from studio system. | platform ratios; accessible preview copy; no-text master. | Shows actual capabilities, original art, approved alt copy; not needed to play. |\n+\n+P0 sequence is shell \u2192 prompt/answer clarity \u2192 feedback/recovery \u2192 responsive\n+variants. No environment tiles, characters, portraits, item icons, effects\n+library, world map, or unrelated game-art family is in scope. For every ID,\n+review at 200% zoom, phone portrait, tablet, desktop, high contrast, reduced\n+motion, and with images disabled; verify mapping, non-colour state, label/alt,\n+safe crop, crispness, provenance/checksum, and no essential text burned into\n+reusable art. Final formats, byte budgets, and store specs await target approval.\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\nindex 80b9199a22884f3ba1a05ef471920526a4e70852..5c9fe5d73c333b34b7a0945f8daa5cae12b06a80\n--- a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\n@@ -12,3 +12,59 @@\n \n Final durations, quantities, loudness targets, loop policy, and generated-cue\n selection need production approval; no audio is generated by this plan.\n+\n+## Original-audio contract and cue IDs\n+\n+Audio reinforces the original *matchday knowledge* arc: invitation, confident\n+answer, rising streak, decisive result, and clear return. It shares the abstract\n+broadcast-studio vocabulary of `01-creative-direction.md` and the journey map\n+in `04-experience-contract.md`: bright electronic percussion, soft claps, warm\n+brass-like synth accents, and abstract crowd-energy texture. It is not a real\n+crowd, chant, anthem, commentary, broadcaster ident, club sound, football-game\n+imitation, or vocal performance associated with a real team.\n+\n+Cue IDs use `AUDIO-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable after package reference.\n+Rendered variants append `-<state>-<mix>`; a manifest records ID, source-session\n+or render checksum, creator/provenance, licence, loop points, loudness/peak,\n+duration, caption/description key, trigger, mix group, and review state.\n+Essential state also has text, icon/pattern, and semantic announcement. Captions\n+describe function (for example, \u201cbrief rising streak cue\u201d); missing audio never\n+blocks an action.\n+\n+P0 is instrumental only: no intelligible vocals, sampled speech, commentary,\n+chants, crowd recordings, or copyrighted musical imitation. Original/properly\n+licensed sources only; generated cues retain settings and receive human\n+originality review.\n+\n+| Stable ID | Purpose, journey, and trigger | Target loop / duration | Acceptance and accessibility |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `AUDIO-MUS-001` | Home/round-choice invitation bed; J0/J2 after screen settles. | Seamless 20\u201340 s loop with clean entry/exit. | Low-distraction music; mute/fade immediately; never masks UI feedback or speech. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-001` | Prompt-ready tick; J1/J2 when an unresolved card is actionable. | One-shot \u22640.5 s. | Caption \u201cQuestion ready\u201d; visible/announced card is complete without it. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-002` | Correct confirmation; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot \u22640.8 s. | Caption \u201cCorrect cue\u201d; distinguishable from incorrect without pitch alone; never precedes written result. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-003` | Incorrect correction; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot \u22640.8 s. | Caption \u201cAnswer correction cue\u201d; calm/non-punitive; explanation remains primary. |\n+| `AUDIO-QZ-004` | Streak threshold rise; J1/J2 on confirmed 3+ streak. | One-shot \u22641.2 s. | Caption \u201cStreak rises\u201d; one per card; suppressible under reduced feedback. |\n+| `AUDIO-RES-001` | Results sting; J1/J2 when results first appear. | One-shot 2\u20134 s, never loops. | Caption \u201cRound complete\u201d; controls available immediately and meaningful muted. |\n+| `AUDIO-SET-001` | Player-requested settings preview; J0 after audio preference change. | One-shot \u22640.5 s. | Obeys current volume/mute; visible labelled test control; never autoplays on Settings open. |\n+| `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Package update ready/applied; J5 at a between-round state only. | One-shot \u22640.7 s. | Caption \u201cUpdate ready/applied\u201d; visible keyboard-accessible status/action. |\n+| `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Save/recovery attention; J3 when recovery panel appears. | One-shot \u22640.7 s. | Caption \u201cSave attention cue\u201d; non-alarming, non-looping, never replaces recovery choices. |\n+\n+## Playback and mixing policy\n+\n+Provide persistent per-local-profile master mute and independent music/feedback\n+controls. Honour platform/system volume, audio focus/interruption, and exposed\n+reduced-sensory preferences. Backgrounding pauses nonessential playback and\n+never affects game state. Do not autoplay audible music before player\n+interaction where platform policy requires it.\n+\n+The same IDs serve responsive web, PWA, Android, and iPhone. Web/PWA waits for\n+audio unlock and silently retains captions/text if unavailable; phones respect\n+mute switch/audio focus. Keyboard, touch, mouse, and gamepad invoke the same\n+semantic state and therefore the same cue. Remote/TV delivery is out of P0.\n+\n+Production tests cover speakers/headphones, system muted, audio unavailable,\n+screen-reader speech, interruption, offline cached assets, and reduced feedback.\n+Acceptance requires intended trigger once at safe state, correct loop/duration,\n+no required audio-only meaning, caption key, mute/volume support, permitted\n+source, and complete manifest provenance/checksum/review. Exact final rendered\n+count, loudness readings, formats, size budget, and language captions await\n+production approval; this plan creates or licenses no audio.\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5882d477494be9f0bd246763ec8d254f593d3d92\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@\n+# 04 \u2014 Experience contract\n+\n+**Traceability:** This contract implements the original *matchday knowledge* challenge in [01-creative-direction.md](01-creative-direction.md) and the first-release systems `GAME-001`\u2013`GAME-012` / journeys `J0`\u2013`J5` in [02-game-design-bible.md](02-game-design-bible.md) and [02-feature-model.md](02-feature-model.md). There is no narrative content model: this is a non-fiction trivia puzzle, whose arc is invitation, confident calls, rising momentum, decisive prompt, then clear celebration or explanation. It must not introduce campaign, battle, characters, or a fictional world.\n+\n+## Product promise and original language\n+\n+The player enters a calm abstract broadcast studio, chooses a compact themed knowledge round, answers one card at a time, and leaves knowing what happened and what was saved. The visual vocabulary is **category fields**, **signal sweeps**, **stat blocks**, **pitch-line geometry**, and **celebration shapes**: original abstract objects rather than a stadium, fixture, presenter, club, competition, or broadcaster. Prompt hierarchy is always question \u2192 answer action \u2192 explanation \u2192 score/streak. Category colour supports scanning but a written category label and a distinct pattern do the semantic work.\n+\n+Tone is precise, lively, adult, inclusive, and fact-first. Instructions use active plain language; correct feedback celebrates the decision, never the person; incorrect feedback explains without shaming. Questions, explanations, captions, error copy, and assets are independently authored. The Athletic and QuizUp establish only topic breadth and short-session outcomes: no marks, questions, wording, screen compositions, visual trade dress, audio, or interaction choreography may be reproduced.\n+\n+## Information architecture and navigation\n+\n+| Area / state | Purpose and primary actions | Navigation and recovery |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Home / local profile | Resume a confirmed paused run; begin `First Whistle`; choose a theme; open settings/help. | Home is the stable return target. Resume identifies the round and last confirmed boundary; a missing run simply omits Resume. |\n+| Round choice | Explain tutorial versus standard round, category, card count, timer mode, and availability. | Select starts only eligible validated content. An empty category says why and offers another eligible theme or Home. |\n+| Quiz / unresolved card | Show progress, question, format-specific answer control, optional pause, and accessible score/streak summary. | One card is actionable. Back/Pause opens a non-modal pause panel at a safe boundary; abandon requires confirmation. |\n+| Resolution / explanation | State correct/incorrect in text, icon, pattern, and optional cue; reveal canonical answer and concise explanation; continue only after state is clear. | Continue advances after a resolved snapshot boundary; no answer can be changed. |\n+| Results | Show answered/correct, score, best active-session streak, category, milestone/save status, then Replay, Choose theme, or Exit. | Reopening is read-only and never awards twice. |\n+| Settings / help | Text size, contrast, reduced motion, captions/descriptions, audio, input help, privacy/diagnostic choice, reset settings, and delete profile. | Available before or during a round; a changed setting takes effect immediately or at the next announced safe boundary. Return preserves the previous route. |\n+| Install/offline/update | Explain install readiness, cached-content state, download need, and a staged update. | Offline compatible content remains playable. Update applies only between rounds; decline/failed update retains the known-good package. |\n+| Recovery / error | Explain a write failure, corrupt draft, incompatible cache, or unexpected fault in plain language. | Offer only applicable Retry, Resume last confirmed state, Continue without saving, Discard draft, Return Home, or Reset cache after save protection. |\n+\n+No first-release account, multiplayer, chat, ranking, purchase, live event, or remote sync route exists. A future connected feature requires a separate identity, reporting, moderation, consent, retention, outage, and safety flow; it must not be implied by this IA.\n+\n+### State, privacy, and destructive-action rules\n+\n+- A disabled Submit names its condition; a typed blank needs a separate explicit \u201cSubmit blank\u201d choice.\n+- No eligible cards, unavailable first offline download, missing optional audio, unsupported gamepad, and unavailable language have explanatory fallback states, never a dead end or silent substitute.\n+- Failed saves keep the prior confirmed snapshot. Corrupt drafts offer the last confirmed snapshot or discard the draft; cache reset is never offered until save protection is reported.\n+- Abandon round, reset settings, and delete profile name their exact effects and offer Cancel as the initial safe action. Delete profile needs a final confirmation, removes local profile/settings/history/snapshots/recovery records/local diagnostics, and returns to first launch.\n+- Optional diagnostics and notifications are off until consent. Their panels state purpose, fields, retention/deletion, and any approved transport; denial never blocks play. P0 never requests names, contacts, location, ad/account IDs, payments, raw typed answers, question text, or save payloads.\n+\n+## Interaction contract by surface\n+\n+Semantic actions are `navigate`, `select`, `submit`, `back`, `pause`, `open-settings`, and `adjust-setting`. Every critical action has an equivalent on each available surface; presentation may adapt but rules/save semantics never do.\n+\n+| Surface | Layout and input choreography | Required adaptation |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Web desktop / laptop | Centered reading column with persistent top progress; pointer hover reveals only nonessential help. | Keyboard works without pointer: `Tab`/`Shift+Tab` follow reading order, Enter/Space activates, arrows move within a radio/ordered group, Escape/Back pauses or closes a non-destructive panel. Browser back never silently abandons a round. |\n+| Web phone / PWA / Android / iPhone | Portrait-first single column; question before answers; sticky but non-obscuring progress/pause row. Landscape is a reflow, not a required orientation. | All primary targets are at least 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px (or platform equivalent), separated to prevent accidental answer selection. No hover dependency; respects system text scaling and safe areas. |\n+| Gamepad | Same single-focus sequence as keyboard; focus lands on page title or first meaningful action after every route/state change. | D-pad/left stick navigates; primary face button selects/submits; secondary backs/closes; Menu/Start pauses. Unsupported/disconnected gamepad is explained while touch/keyboard remain available. |\n+| Mouse / trackpad | Pointer targets match visible controls; hover only supplements labels/tooltips. | Click has an equivalent keyboard action; focus remains visible after a click. |\n+| Screen reader, switch, voice, assistive input | Native semantic controls are preferred over canvas-only controls; actions have stable accessible names. | Voice can invoke visible unique labels such as \u201cSubmit answer\u201d and \u201cPause round\u201d; it need not parse football answers as commands. Switch uses the same finite focus order. Status changes announce once without stealing focus. |\n+\n+Remote-control/TV input is not a selected delivery target; it remains an approval item rather than implied P0 scope.\n+\n+## Responsive visual behaviour and tokens\n+\n+Use a portrait-first single-column core. At narrow widths, full-width answer controls stack. At tablet width, score/streak may sit beside the prompt only when reading measure and answer target size are preserved. At desktop width, cap the reading column; spare space is quiet studio texture, never a competing task. Reflow at browser zoom and system text enlargement; never truncate question, explanation, confirmation, or recovery copy.\n+\n+Tokens are semantic and product-specific: `FT-SPACE-1..6`, `FT-TYPE-PROMPT`, `FT-TYPE-BODY`, `FT-TYPE-NUMERIC`, `FT-SURFACE-BASE`, `FT-SURFACE-CATEGORY-{world,domestic,club,records}`, `FT-STATE-{focus,correct,incorrect,warning}`, `FT-PATTERN-{field,grid,sweep}`, and `FT-MOTION-{none,brief,celebrate}`. Normal text meets 4.5:1 (3:1 only for large text); essential icons, focus indicators, and control boundaries meet 3:1. High contrast uses tested semantic tokens, not saturation alone.\n+\n+Correct/incorrect combines a written result, icon, pattern/border, and optional audio. Focus is a high-contrast non-colour-only outline, never hidden behind sticky UI. Motion defaults to short non-flashing transitions; reduced motion replaces signal sweeps, card movement, and celebration bursts with immediate state changes. No animation flashes more than three times per second.\n+\n+## Accessibility and content requirements\n+\n+- Each route has one programmatic page title/heading and landmarks for header, main quiz, and complementary progress. Dialogs label their consequence, trap focus only while open, and restore focus to the invoker.\n+- Answer groups expose question text, format, selected state, position, and enabled/disabled reason. Score/streak labels are concise; progress exposes ordinal and total.\n+- Resolution uses a polite live region for outcome/score; blocking errors use assertive announcement only when action cannot continue. Captions/descriptions are visible on request and every cue has text. Decorative studio art is hidden from assistive tech.\n+- Text size persists and honours system scaling. Localisation externalises prompts, answers, explanations, categories, recovery/error strings, captions, and labels; a language is not selectable until aliases and factual review pass.\n+- Timer mode defaults off. If later enabled it states duration, has a non-timed alternative, offers extension/pause where applicable, and never prevents an explanation.\n+\n+## Journey-to-presentation map and acceptance\n+\n+| Journey | Location/screen state | Shared visual/audio IDs | Acceptance |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| J0 | Home, Settings, consent | `ASSET-SHL-001`, `ASSET-UI-001`, `AUDIO-SET-001` | Settings apply globally; consent denial remains playable; labels/focus order work. |\n+| J1 | First Whistle, prompt, resolution, results | `ASSET-QZ-001`, `ASSET-FBK-001..004`, `AUDIO-QZ-001..004` | Offline tutorial completes with readable non-colour feedback and confirmed save. |\n+| J2 | Theme choice, standard round, unavailable-theme empty state | `ASSET-QZ-002`, `AUDIO-QZ-001..003` | Eligible choice, clear empty state, replay/exit without social comparison. |\n+| J3 | Pause, save failure, recovery, delete confirmation | `ASSET-UI-003`, `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Prior confirmed state is protected; destructive choices are explicit/cancellable. |\n+| J4 | Editorial/release workflow, not player runtime | `ASSET-OPS-001` | Missing provenance or ambiguous answers block publish. |\n+| J5 | Download/update/error/recovery | `ASSET-SYS-001`, `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Safe-boundary update, offline fallback, retry/home, privacy-preserving diagnostic choice are clear. |\n+\n+Before release, verify each row with keyboard, touch, screen reader, system text enlargement, high contrast, reduced motion, muted audio/captions, offline cached content, failed save, corrupt draft, and deletion. Final browser/OS/device/performance matrix remains an approval gate in `03-technical-contract.md`.\n\ntokens used\n63,713\n", "adapter_log": "", "test_log": "Diff whitespace and identifier trace checks exited successfully.", "browser_log": "Not applicable: documentation-only change.", "screenshots": []}, "acceptance_results": [{"criterion": "Navigation, empty/error states, feedback, destructive actions, and privacy-sensitive content are specified.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Experience contract defines IA, fallback/error and recovery states, feedback, destructive confirmations, and diagnostic/privacy consent."}, {"criterion": "Tokens, keyboard behaviour, focus, screen-reader labels, contrast, touch targets, and reduced motion are defined.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Defines semantic tokens, keyboard/gamepad mappings, focus/live-region rules, 4.5:1 contrast, 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px targets, and reduced-motion behaviour."}, {"criterion": "The proposed experience is original and does not reproduce a reference product's trade dress.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Contracts require an original abstract broadcast-studio identity and prohibit copied marks, layouts, copy, assets, and choreography."}, {"criterion": "Where visual assets are in scope, the asset plan assigns stable, product-specific asset-family IDs, purpose, variants, provenance/originality, accessibility, and acceptance requirements.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Asset direction assigns ASSET-SHL/QZ/UI/FBK/SYS/OPS/MKT IDs with variants, provenance, accessibility, priority, and review rules."}, {"criterion": "Where audio is in scope, the cue map assigns stable, product-specific cue IDs and purpose, loop/duration, interaction trigger, and acceptance requirements.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Audio direction defines AUDIO-MUS/QZ/RES/SET/SYS IDs with triggers, duration/loop targets, captions, mixing, provenance, and acceptance."}, {"criterion": "For every game and narrative-led product, creative, narrative, visual, and audio documents share a traceable premise/tone/content vocabulary and map their first-release locations, characters, scenes, UI states, and cues to user/player journeys.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "The experience contract maps the non-fiction matchday-knowledge premise and J0\u2013J5 UI states to asset/audio IDs; asset/audio documents share that vocabulary and explicitly exclude fictional scenes/characters."}], "documentation": {"reviewed_files": ["projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md", "projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md", "projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md", "projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/03-technical-contract.md"], "updated_files": ["projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md", "projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md", "projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md"], "summary": "Added the requested experience contract and expanded existing asset/audio direction. README was not changed because no setup, command, architecture, or implemented product behaviour changed."}, "known_limitations": ["Final support matrix, performance/download budgets, store requirements, rendered audio/loudness measurements, and language selection remain existing approval gates."], "browser_coverage": "No Playwright spec changed because this is documentation-only domain-contract work without browser implementation.", "recommended_next_step": "complete"}


